From 4ab5f0d7f34e41b85c9d552aaaacb4705b41cdcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ArifiLabs <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:00:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: README, STATUS, X1 notes and NOTICE state each figure
 at its receipt's precision and correct six overstatements

Speed figures are now the receipts' own values: medians for seven pairs and means for ROCmFP4-FAST, said once under
the table, with percents cut to one decimal and never rounded up. File sizes are GB from each file's byte count
(14.56, 13.22, 17.38, 26.14 GB; the old 16.2 and 24.3 were GiB). The TQ rows are labelled as llama-bench results.

Six statements become what the code and the receipts show. Six mat-vec changes to upstream formats run on every
Vulkan device, and the README now names them instead of promising upstream paths elsewhere. The 890M placement
gives the host split per file instead of "fully into GPU memory". The quality line names its two gates and the
ROCmFP4 opt-in residual. The provenance line gives the grandfathered and exempt counts. The FA dequant-KV row quotes
the amended same-binary contrast instead of the +8.1% that did not reproduce. NOTICE and licenses/README.md record
the one ciru CMake change that is carried.

The MoE section names the Vulkan expert cache beside PowerInfer streaming with no speed claim, and its measured
cost on one memory pool joins the STATUS non-results. TheTom and FreeToken are credited for what this tree carries.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release documents for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documents only; no code path is touched.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
